{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_3a406e22797249209e4e0be2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GSQ-RCO IQ3_S","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_7c38f86257674661a77e6b72","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np = \"/work/432hs-app/PLAN.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\nfor n in (16, 17, 18, 19):\n    old = f\"{n}. [ ] \"\n    assert old in s\n    s = s.replace(old, f\"{n}. [x] \", 1)\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\n\nr = \"/work/432hs-app/AGENT_REPORT.md\"\ns = open(r).read()\nold = \"\"\"## Build & test commands (run in /work/432hs-app)\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"## Follow-up batch 2 (2026-11-08, from Jason's Note10+ field test)\n\nOn-device evidence: pressing Back left the viewModelScope job decoding\nunseen; at 21:52:20 Samsung's FreecessController froze the backgrounded\nprocess (`state: Freezeable -> Frozen, Reason: Bg`), the temp\n`converted.m4a` froze at 7.7 MB and was never finalised (no moov) nor\nsaved. Fix below.\n\n### (1) Conversion now runs in a foreground service\n\n`ConvertService` (started with `ContextCompat.startForegroundService`)\nperforms decode → shift → encode → save on its own worker thread:\n\n- **FGS type**: `mediaProcessing` is the natural fit but the installed\n  android-34 platform exposes no `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_MEDIA_PROCESSING`\n  (absent from both `ServiceInfo` in android.jar and the framework attr\n  enums — AAPT rejected `foregroundServiceType=\\\"mediaProcessing\\\"`), so the\n  task's sanctioned fallback is used: `dataSync` +\n  `FOREGROUND_SERVICE(_DATA_SYNC)` permissions. Note: Android 14 limits\n  dataSync FGS to ~10 min per 24 h — fine for minutes-long conversions,\n  but switch back to `mediaProcessing` whenever the compile platform\n  ships it.\n- **Progress notification**: low-importance channel \"Conversions\",\n  progress bar updated on integer-percent changes, tap opens MainActivity.\n  POST_NOTIFICATIONS is requested at Convert time on API 33+; **the\n  callback converts either way** — with the permission denied the shade\n  simply shows nothing, the service and wake lock still do their job.\n- **Wake lock**: PARTIAL_WAKE_LOCK (`audio432:conversion`, 2 h safety\n  timeout), released in the finally-block on finish/fail and in\n  `onDestroy`; `stopForeground(REMOVE)` + `stopSelf()` there as well.\n- A frozen-then-resumed service can also no longer strand a temp file:\n  see (encoder below).\n\n### (1b) Encoder always finalises or deletes\n\n`AudioEncoder.encode` now calls **`muxer.stop()` before `release()`** on\nsuccess (writes the moov index — release alone can leave an unplayable\nfile), and on *any* failure (exception mid-drain) **deletes the partial\nout file**. The service additionally deletes `cache/converted.m4a` in its\nown catch, so a half-written 7.7 MB container can never be offered to\nthe user.\n\n### (2) State survives Back / reopen / recreation\n\n`media/ConversionRepository` — a process-level `StateFlow<ConversionState>`\n(phase IDLE/RUNNING/DONE/FAILED, progress, status, inputUri, outputUri,\noutputName). The *service* writes it; `ConvertViewModel` collects it in\n`init`, so a ViewModel created after Back or an Activity recreation\nimmediately re-attaches to the live progress or the last result. The\nscreen then shows the running progress bar/status again, or \"Saved to…\"\nwith the result and auto-opens the player; the file line shows the input\n\"(from last conversion)\". Back no longer cancels the work — nothing\nconversion-related runs in `viewModelScope` anymore.\n\n### (3) Tuning detection: low-confidence guess + bass/percussion filtering\n\n- **Best guess always offered**: low confidence now keeps the guess in\n  state and shows \"Tuning unclear: best guess A≈441.0 Hz (confidence\n  0.18), using 440\" plus a **\"Use detected A≈441.0 Hz\"** button that\n  fills the From field. Confident detections still auto-fill.\n- **200–2000 Hz focus** (`minHz` default 80 → 200): 808 bass and kick\n  content carries little reliable tuning information.\n- **Sustained-peak gate**: a peak votes only if the same pitch (within\n  3 FFT bins) appears in ≥ 3 consecutive frames of the same analysis\n  window; one-off drum/plosive transients drop out. Weight scaled by\n  √sustain so longer-lived partials dominate.\n- New JVM test `tunedTonesWinOverSweepPercussionAndNoise`: sustained\n  A=444 chord + sliding 40–190 Hz sweep + percussive noise bursts every\n  250 ms + hiss bed → **detected 444.004 Hz, confidence 0.998**. The old\n  432/440/444 chord and 432-tone tests still pass unchanged (1.000).\n\n## Build & test commands (run in /work/432hs-app)\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\n\nold = \"\"\"- `./gradlew test` — **BUILD SUCCESSFUL; 20 unit tests, 0 failures**\n  (debug + release variants): DspTest 10, TuningDetectorTest 5,\n  AbSwitchTest 3, ConverterTest 1, TimeFormatTest 1.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"- `./gradlew test` — **BUILD SUCCESSFUL; 21 unit tests, 0 failures**\n  (debug + release variants): DspTest 10, TuningDetectorTest 6,\n  AbSwitchTest 3, ConverterTest 1, TimeFormatTest 1.\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\n\nold = \"\"\"## Unverified / uncertain\n- **No device install possible in this sandbox** (and per instructions\n  nothing was installed on a phone). Tuning detection on *real* music,\n  the MediaPlayer/A-B behavior, rotation survival, Downloads saving and\n  share intents are compile-verified only.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"## Unverified / uncertain — what still needs on-device checking\n- **No device install possible in this sandbox** (and per instructions\n  nothing was installed on a phone). Everything in batch 2 — service\n  actually beating Samsung's freezer mid-encode, wake-lock behavior,\n  notification visible/denied paths, the dataSync FGS start from the\n  Activity on One UI 4, state re-attach after Back, the guess button on\n  the real hip-hop FLAC — is compile-verified only.\n- Tuning detection on *real* music, the MediaPlayer/A-B behavior,\n  rotation survival, Downloads saving and share intents were already\n  device-checked only indirectly (Jason's run); re-check after this build.\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new, 1)\nopen(r, \"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF","description":"Tick plan steps 16-19 and append batch-2 section to AGENT_REPORT.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92355,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bbac423-c721-4d38-aad7-f0828aa806c1","uuid":"43eb6428-9741-4ac5-9fb5-48dcd7715777","timestamp":"2026-11-08T12:03:49.297Z"}
