{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_94d5841f0ae042118c4f961f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GSQ-RCO IQ3_S","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a1b4099a05f84ecea7b20294","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status --short && G=\"git -c user.name=agent -c user.email=agent@local\" && \\\n$G add app/src/main/java/com/agent/audio432/media/ConversionRepository.kt app/src/main/java/com/agent/audio432/media/AudioEncoder.kt && \\\n$G commit -q -m \"Finalize or delete the encoded file; add process-wide conversion state\n\nAudioEncoder now calls MediaMuxer.stop() before release() so the moov\nindex is always written, and deletes the partial container on any\nfailure. ConversionRepository holds phase/progress/status/URIs in a\nprocess-level StateFlow: the service writes it, any later ViewModel\nre-attaches, so Back or a recreation never loses a running conversion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && \\\n$G add app/src/main/java/com/agent/audio432/ConvertService.kt app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_stat_convert.xml && \\\n$G commit -q -m \"Run conversions in a foreground service with notification and wake lock\n\nSamsung's background freezer froze a mid-encode job on the Note10+ and\nthe temp m4a was never finalised. The whole decode/shift/encode/save now\nruns in ConvertService: startForeground with dataSync type (the installed\nandroid-34 platform lacks FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_MEDIA_PROCESSING; AAPT\nrejects it - documented fallback), progress notification on a LOW channel\nPOST_NOTIFICATIONS never gates the conversion itself, and a partial wake\nlock with a 2 h safety timeout that is released on finish/fail/onDestroy\ntogether with stopForeground + stopSelf.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && \\\n$G add app/src/main/java/com/agent/audio432/dsp/TuningDetector.kt app/src/test/java/com/agent/audio432/dsp/TuningDetectorTest.kt && \\\n$G commit -q -m \"Tuning detector: 200 Hz floor and sustained-peak gate\n\nReal hip-hop FLAC scored only 0.18. Peaks are now only counted between\n200-2000 Hz (808 bass/kick carry no reliable tuning cue) and must\npersist in >= 3 consecutive frames (within 3 bins, weight * sqrt of\nsustain) so one-off drum transients drop out. New stress test: sustained\nA=444 chord vs 40-190 Hz sweep + percussive bursts + hiss bed detects\n444.004 Hz at confidence 0.998; the original 432/440/444 tests stay green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","description":"Commit repository, service, manifest, detector and tests"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":95413,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bbac423-c721-4d38-aad7-f0828aa806c1","uuid":"7ade1469-6f10-467e-8378-3eefb6cebd49","timestamp":"2026-11-08T12:03:57.541Z"}
